7c-8650-5b8b-a2a5-255818e1f719" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542353 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542358 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542353 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542353 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$, if $4{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542353 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "036a544e-adcf-5604-8565-d9b2d689152b" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542353 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get\n\n$$\n2k=-8\\,⟹\\,k=-4.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that $4{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542366 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542355 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542366 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542366 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$, if $3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542366 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e5e9f97a-8dbd-5e5f-adc8-0ae163476518" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542366 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get\n\n$$\n3k=-6\\,⟹\\,k=-2.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that $3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542367 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186119805.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542367 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "654ebed8-c886-576a-ae1a-ac9f64553608" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
